-- akn:att_5__hc_1 Annex E, the form for asking the exceptions committee to leave the reform (sent by 31.1.2021; employee and institution details, the request, the owner's comments); its rule is 3.6's.

§§ `נספח ו' אפשרויות העסקה לפי בסיסי המשרה`

-- Annex F's table. Its columns, as the corpus prints the headings (¶1-¶5):
-- serial, post, job base, the position in percent (its asterisk, ¶61: "as
-- far as she works Sunday to Thursday 7:55-14:00 and Friday 7:55-12:45;
-- where the kindergarten's hours differ, so does the position"), the
-- weekly hours actually worked, and notes.
DECLARE `annex F row` HAS
    `annex F serial`        IS A NUMBER
    `annex F post`          IS A STRING
    `annex F base`          IS A NUMBER
    `annex F percent`       IS A NUMBER        @desc the position as printed, in percent
    `annex F hours worked`  IS A MAYBE NUMBER  @desc the weekly hours actually worked, NOTHING where the cell is blank

-- The corpus publishes the table as loose lines with each row's cells out
-- of order and its notes broken across lines, so which figure sits in
-- which column of which row is not something its text says (MMS-424).
-- The rows are an input until the corpus publishes the table and is
-- re-synced. The notes that read as prose are encoded below.
@ref akn:att_6__hc_1
@desc Annex F's rows, one per printed row in the printed order. The corpus publishes this table scrambled (MMS-424), so the values are supplied from outside until the corpus is fixed and re-synced.
ASSUME `annex F's rows` IS A LIST OF `annex F row`

-- The empty row stands for a serial the table does not print.
GIVEN l IS A LIST OF `annex F row`
GIVETH AN `annex F row`
DECIDE `the first annex F row of` l IS
    CONSIDER l
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `annex F row` 0 "" 0 0 NOTHING
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN r

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, l IS A LIST OF `annex F row`
GIVETH AN `annex F row`
DECIDE `the annex F row numbered` n `in` l IS
    `the first annex F row of` (filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `annex F serial` EQUALS n) l)

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `annex F row`
DECIDE `annex F row number` n IS
    `the annex F row numbered` n `in` `annex F's rows`

-- PLACEHOLDER rows (invented figures, not the table's) for the lookup.
`placeholder annex F rows` MEANS
    LIST `annex F row` 1 "placeholder post" 10 100 (JUST 10),
         `annex F row` 2 "placeholder post" 20 50  NOTHING

#ASSERT (`the annex F row numbered` 2 `in` `placeholder annex F rows`)'s `annex F base` EQUALS 20
#ASSERT (`the annex F row numbered` 3 `in` `placeholder annex F rows`)'s `annex F serial` EQUALS 0

-- Row 4's note (¶15-¶17): "a complementary teacher who works 5 days a
-- week, 6.08 each day, her position will be up to 90% only, as she
-- actually works 30.4 weekly hours". The week the notes assume.
@ref akn:att_6__hc_1/p15 akn:att_6__hc_1/p16 akn:att_6__hc_1/p17
`five days of the 14:00 kindergarten` MEANS 30.4
`the complementary teacher's position in row 4's note, in percent` MEANS 90

#ASSERT 5 TIMES 6.08 EQUALS `five days of the 14:00 kindergarten`

GIVEN `percent` IS A NUMBER, `share` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `matches the printed percent` `percent` `share` IF
        (`share` TIMES 100) MINUS `percent` AT MOST 0.1
    AND `percent` MINUS (`share` TIMES 100) AT MOST 0.1

-- F-2020-21_tashpa_04-a: annex F's arithmetic does not run on 4.1.1's
-- base. Row 4's note puts the complementary teacher's 30.4 hours at 90%;
-- on 4.1.1's base for her (33.4, under 50) 30.4 hours are 91%.
`annex F's note puts 30.4 hours at a position 4.1.1's base does not give` MEANS
        NOT `matches the printed percent`
                `the complementary teacher's position in row 4's note, in percent`
                (`position by the base` `five days of the 14:00 kindergarten` (`job base` `under 50` `a complementary teacher`))
    AND `matches the printed percent` 91 (`position by the base` `five days of the 14:00 kindergarten` (`job base` `under 50` `a complementary teacher`))
#ASSERT `annex F's note puts 30.4 hours at a position 4.1.1's base does not give`

-- The reading adopted (F-2020-21_tashpa_04-a): 4.1.1, the clause that
-- sets the job base, governs; annex F is read as an illustration of
-- 4.1.5's arithmetic, which this file computes on 4.1.1's bases.

§§ `Worked examples`

-- Ages, seniority and positions are placeholders.
`an existing managing teacher of 56` MEANS
    `kindergarten teacher` WITH
        `recognised years of actual teaching` IS 30
        `seniority in teaching`              IS 30
        `academic`                           IS TRUE
        `certified to teach`                 IS TRUE
        `position fraction`                  IS 1
        `signed the academic-studies commitment` IS FALSE
        `approved as an exception`           IS FALSE
        `an intern`                          IS FALSE
        `a health professional`              IS FALSE
        `a cluster manager`                  IS FALSE
        `age on 31 December`                 IS 56

#ASSERT `job base` (`the age band of` `an existing managing teacher of 56`) `the kindergarten's managing teacher` EQUALS 26.8
#ASSERT `age hours off the base` `an existing managing teacher of 56` EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `joins the reform` `an existing managing teacher of 56`
#ASSERT `joins the reform` `a new academic at 40%`
#ASSERT NOT `employed at that scope on the reform` `a new academic at 40%` FALSE 0.4
#ASSERT `the Ministry approves the owner's joining` 25 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Ministry approves the owner's joining` 40 TRUE
#ASSERT `a mother kindergarten teacher's position` 1 TRUE EQUALS 1.1
#ASSERT `the אופק חדש advance` `an academic kindergarten teacher` 10000 1 EQUALS 1600
#ASSERT `end of the day Sunday to Thursday` `autism` EQUALS 1005
#ASSERT `age hours off a part position` `an existing teacher of 52 at half a position` EQUALS 1

#TRACE `sending the commitment` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `send the commitment through the portal` AT 20
#TRACE `sending the commitment` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Ministry of Education` DOES `impose sanctions on the owner` AT 45
#TRACE `sending the staff file` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `send the staff file through the portal` AT 70
#TRACE `filing the academic-studies commitment` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `file the academic-studies commitment` AT 50
#TRACE `no placement above 126% or 42 hours` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `place a kindergarten teacher above the ceiling` 1.2 43 AT 10
